      "message": "According to https://source.android.com/docs/core/connect/bluetooth/hci_requirements#le-multi-advertising-state-change-sub-event this is only ever 0\n\nI\u0027d suggest that we either:\n- Define an enum for this:\n  enum VseStateChangeReason : 8 {\n    CONNECTION_RECEIVED \u003d 0x00,\n  }\n  \n  packet LEAdvertiseStateChangeEvent : VendorSpecificEvent (subevent_code \u003d BLE_STCHANGE) {\n    advertising_instance : 8,\n    state_change_reason : VseStateChangeReason,\n    connection_handle: 12,\n    _reserved_ : 4,\n  }\n  \n- Make it fixed:\n  packet LEAdvertiseStateChangeEvent : VendorSpecificEvent (subevent_code \u003d BLE_STCHANGE) {\n    advertising_instance : 8,\n    _fixed_ \u003d 0 : 8, // Connection received\n    connection_handle: 12,\n    _reserved_ : 4,\n  }\n  \n  Either way, I think the connection handle should just be 12 bits.\n  \n  Thanks!",
